# openc2e-derived Buddy Life substrate

The files in this `buddy_life/` directory are a Godot/GDScript compatibility port derived
from behavioral algorithms and data structures in the openc2e project.

- Upstream project: `openc2e/openc2e`
- Reviewed upstream revision: `6a4396c83152fe9f9152be924b5a8edc8e759a6a`
- Upstream license: GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1 or later
- Port license: GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1 or later
- Port date: 2026-07-29

The port covers the independently packaged biological library only:

- 256 normalized chemicals and C2e half-life decay (`buddy_biology_chemical_pool.gd`);
- ATP/ADP energy accounting, injury and organ life force (`buddy_biology_organ.gd`);
- reactions, emitters, receptors and loci (`buddy_biology_organ.gd`);
- 48-byte state-variable rules (`buddy_biology_sv_rule.gd`);
- brain lobes, neurons, tracts and dendrites (`buddy_biology_brain.gd`);
- instinct processing (`buddy_biology_instinct.gd`);
- genes and their life-stage switch-on (`buddy_genome.gd`);
- persistent substrate state and the bridge to Prismtek Buddy Core
  (`buddy_biology_substrate.gd`).

It does **not** include openc2e rendering, SDL world execution, CAOS, original
Creatures game data, genomes, sprites, sounds or other proprietary assets.

Each source file carries an SPDX `LGPL-2.1-or-later` identifier. The complete
license text and the redistribution terms this module is offered under are in
`LICENSE.md` beside this file; `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` at the package root records
the same attribution for the Buddy Core package as a whole.

Because the module ships as GDScript source inside this repository and inside every
exported pack, the corresponding source required by the LGPL travels with each
distributed build. Retain this notice, `LICENSE.md`, and the SPDX headers when
redistributing the module or a modified version.

